+# DS preview conventions
+
+Task 002 confirmation for where this iteration's repo-side DS previews live and what each self-contained preview head must include.
+
+## Repo location decision
+
+Use the preferred `design-system/` mirror directory for all new or changed preview deliverables in this iteration.
+
+Existing `spikes/ds-convert/` files remain useful reference material for the phase-2 daisyUI conversion style, but they are not the delivery location for this iteration. The mirror keeps the eventual DesignSync push mechanical: remove the `design-system/` prefix and push the same relative path into the cloud DS project.
+
+| Repo path | Cloud DS path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `design-system/wireframes/invite-a-member.html` | `wireframes/invite-a-member.html` | Invite-a-member preview, showing the member-admin and staff/admin variants together unless task 003 finds two sibling files render clearer. |
+| `design-system/wireframes/profile-completion.html` | `wireframes/profile-completion.html` | Invited-member profile completion preview. |
+| `design-system/wireframes/auth-check-email.html` | `wireframes/auth-check-email.html` | Sign-in check-email and auth delivery-progress preview. |
+| `design-system/components/badges/badges.card.html` | `components/badges/badges.card.html` | Badges component card with the role / Membership-Admin chips added. |
+
+If the invite variants are split during task 003 for readability, use sibling files under the same directory (`design-system/wireframes/invite-a-member-member-admin.html` and `design-system/wireframes/invite-a-member-staff.html`) with the same prefix-stripping mapping.
+
+## Relative asset paths
+
+Author paths as if `design-system/` is the DS root:
+
+- From `design-system/wireframes/*.html` to DS root assets: `../brand/...`.
+- From `design-system/components/badges/*.html` to DS root assets: `../../brand/...`.
+- Prefer inline SVGs, text marks, initials, or CSS-only marks where that is enough to mirror the shipped surface; do not point previews at Phoenix app static paths.
+- Do not link `styles.css`, `memba.css`, or the app build output. Each preview must carry the CDN links and CSS it needs.
+
+## Self-contained head block
+
+Paste this shape into each new preview and adjust only the `<title>` plus page-specific raw tokens/layout CSS. The `:root` variables are copied from `web/assets/css/app.css`; keep them in sync if the app theme changes.
+
